# Text files are LF, except Doorstop's settings file, which keeps the CRLF
# of the file it copies. The PNGs are declared binary.
#
# Declaring the PNGs binary matters: this repository holds the icon and every
# picture the wheel is drawn with. If git ever treated one as text it would
# corrupt it, and nobody would notice until the mod manager or the game
# showed it.
#
# Pinning LF keeps diffs readable. Without it, a checkout on a machine with
# other line endings can rewrite every line, and a real change gets lost in
# the noise.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.cs       text eol=lf
*.csproj   text eol=lf
*.props    text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf
*.ps1      text eol=lf

*.txt      text eol=lf
*.ini      text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
